{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interiorMarkov_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interiorMarkov_apply","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InteriorMarkovFromBraid.lean#L225-L235","doc":"The same statement with the membership hypotheses as arguments rather than\nbounded quantifiers, for convenience at call sites.\n\nDeliberately **not** named `interiorMarkov_of_braided`: that name belongs to\n`QOU.Hecke.InteriorMarkovOfBraidedTower`, on the `MarkovTower` carrier, and two\ndeclarations sharing it across carriers is the overload defect this corpus has\nalready paid for once with `markovZ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interiorMarkov_shiftedUpTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interiorMarkov_shiftedUpTo","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InteriorMarkovFromBraid.lean#L185-L223","doc":"**The interior-bond Markov property, stage by stage, from the braid\nrelations.**\n\nFor every `g` and `M`, every `a ∈ H g` and every `b` in the stage\n`shiftedUpTo (g+1) M` of the tail above `g`:\n\n    tr (a * g g * b) = z * tr (a * b).\n\nThis is `qou-gr3t`'s `InteriorMarkov` — the property its counter-model shows is\n*independent of the tower axioms* — derived from `BraidedTower` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interior_span_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interior_span_step","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InteriorMarkovFromBraid.lean#L149-L183","doc":"The sandwich half of the induction step, as a standalone lemma so that the\n`span_induction` runs in a context mentioning nothing but `s`.\n\nBoth sides peel `g (M+1)` with the same two-sided Markov step, so they agree as\nsoon as the inductive hypothesis handles the shortened word `v * w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interior_of_mem_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.interior_of_mem_bot","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InteriorMarkovFromBraid.lean#L135-L147","doc":"The interior-bond rule on a stage that is `⊥`: `b` is a scalar, and the\nclaim is the Markov axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.shiftedUpTo_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InteriorMarkovFromBraid.shiftedUpTo_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InteriorMarkovFromBraid.lean#L126-L133","doc":"A stage whose generator window is empty is `⊥`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}